{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"64b843c887c82f8b4539e800ead2a80d401c1773d262217a2a7e2ff3250737ea","packTokens":7182,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":678,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":907,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":5460,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace phone/email-based parts ordering with a self-service ordering portal\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Allow customers to quickly find parts using part numbers, product names, categories, and vehicle information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Show each customer their applicable pricing and current stock availability\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Reduce manual order-entry work for office staff\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Give customers visibility into order status and invoices\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff with operational order queues and delivery information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide management with basic sales and product reporting\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Maintain an auditable history of orders, invoices, customer accounts, and catalogue changes\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer authentication with sign-in, password reset, and account management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Build product catalogue with search, filtering, categories, and vehicle compatibility\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer-specific pricing and price list management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Manage stock availability with ERP CSV imports\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Build basket and checkout workflow with delivery date rules\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement order management with status tracking and staff editing capabilities\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Build customer order history, cancellation, and repeat order functionality\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement invoice creation, viewing, PDF download, and payment tracking\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Build administrative tools for product, user, category, and price list management\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Is the Customer Account Manager role part of the first release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No: first release has Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator only\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Does a Buyer see every order and invoice of their company, or only the ones they placed? The Buyer section says 'their company's orders', but the Account Manager role adds 'orders placed by other users'.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Buyer sees all orders and invoices of their own company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which status changes can staff make after confirmation? Can they skip a status, go back a step, or cancel a Confirmed or Picking order?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Forward only, in order (Confirmed → Picking → Out for delivery → Delivered); staff may cancel any order not yet Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Under 'where permitted', when may staff change the delivery date or address before confirmation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Always before confirmation, limited to the customer's addresses and dates valid under the cutoff rule\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What happens to a customer company's users and open orders when the company is set inactive?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Its users cannot sign in or order; existing orders and invoices stay visible to staff\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Buyers see all of their company's orders (answer Q-2). Can a Buyer also cancel or repeat a Received order that a colleague placed, or that staff created for the company?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any Buyer of the company may cancel or repeat any company order that is eligible\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"With no Customer Account Manager in the first release (answer Q-1), can Buyers add or edit their company's delivery addresses, or do only staff/admins manage them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only staff/admins manage addresses; Buyers choose from existing ones\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"For an inactive customer company (answer Q-5), can staff still move its open orders forward, create new orders for it, and have invoices created when its orders are delivered?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Open orders continue as normal and invoices are still created; staff cannot create new orders for the company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall authenticate users by email and password, starting a session and returning the user's role when credentials match an active account.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject sign-in attempts with unknown emails or wrong passwords using one identical invalid-credentials error and no session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall lock an account for 15 minutes after 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, rejecting all attempts during the lock with a temporary-lock error, and reset the failure count after a successful sign-in.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject sign-in and all existing-session requests, including order submission, for deactivated users or users of inactive companies.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall invalidate a user's session token when the user signs out.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject with 401 and no record data any request to endpoints other than sign-in, password reset, and invitation acceptance that lacks a valid session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject with 403 any request to an endpoint outside the capabilities of the caller's role, with Administrators including all Office Staff capabilities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall restrict a signed-in Buyer to orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses, and account data of their own company, returning 404 for other companies' records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall respond identically to password reset requests regardless of whether the email exists, sending a single-use reset link valid for a configured period (default 1 hour) only when the account is active (or temporarily locked) and its company, if any, is active.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let a user set a new password via an unexpired, unused reset link, replacing the password, invalidating the link, and clearing any sign-in lock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject password changes via expired, used, or otherwise invalid reset links (pending, deactivated, or inactive-company users), leaving the password and any lock unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators invite Buyers (linked to a company) or Office Staff, creating a pending account and sending an invitation link valid for a configured period (default 7 days).\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators invite users with the Administrator role, creating a pending account and sending an invitation email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall activate an invited user's account when they set a password via an unexpired invitation link.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators resend invitations, invalidating all previous invitation links for that user and sending a new invitation email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators list users with role, company, and status, assign a Buyer to a company, and deactivate or reactivate users without deleting their orders or invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators change a user's role between Buyer and Office Staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators change a user's role to Administrator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject reactivation of a deactivated user whose company is inactive.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return, for a Buyer's catalogue text search, active products whose name, code, part number, or brand contains the term, case-insensitively.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Buyers filter the catalogue by category, combined with search terms, and return all active products once the filter is cleared.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return active products matching all supplied vehicle search criteria (make, model, year, engine, fuel type, variant) via compatibility entries.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return, for Buyer catalogue listings, only active products with image, name, code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, Buyer price, and stock status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return, when a Buyer opens an active product, its image, name, code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, price, stock status, and compatible vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall price products and order/basket lines from the price list currently assigned to the Buyer's company at request time, reflecting assignment changes immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff view the price a company pays for a product from its assigned price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show 'Price on request' for products lacking a price on the company's price list and reject adding such products to a basket or order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators create, rename, and deactivate price lists, manage product prices on them, and assign an active price list to a company.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall keep unit prices on existing orders and invoices unchanged when price lists or company assignments later change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall derive stock status as Out of stock, Low stock, or In stock based on imported quantity relative to a configured low-stock threshold.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall update stock quantities and statuses from a valid scheduled ERP CSV import and log a successful import with row counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall skip unknown product rows in a valid CSV import, applying other rows and logging the skipped identifiers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall leave stock quantities unchanged and log a failed import when the CSV file is missing, unreadable, empty, or invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let staff and administrators list stock imports with time, status, rows applied, skipped identifiers, and failure reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall not send create, update, or delete requests to the ERP system.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show staff, when opening a product, its imported quantity, stock status, last successful import time, and prices on each price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject basket, order, or amendment quantities exceeding available stock or for out-of-stock products, stating the available quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall maintain a session-scoped Buyer basket supporting adding, quantity changes (minimum 1), and line removal, returning line and subtotal totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date based on cutoff time, timezone, and non-working dates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall accept only valid selectable delivery dates for baskets and orders, checked at submission, rejecting others with an error naming the date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject delivery addresses not belonging to the order's company, naming the delivery address field.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall re-check availability, stock, and pricing at order submission, rejecting and listing affected lines if any have changed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show a final checkout review page with lines, prices, totals, address, date, and note before submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall create a new order with a sequential number, order-time prices, address copy, date, note, status Received, and first timeline entry, then empty the basket.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject order submissions from inactive companies or deactivated users and reject staff order creation for inactive companies.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall append a timeline entry with status, timestamp, and actor whenever an order's status changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall send order emails to the placing Buyer if still active and linked to the company, otherwise to the company's contact email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return, for a Buyer's order list, all company orders including colleagues' and staff-created ones, filterable by status and date range.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return full order details (number, dates, address, status, timeline, lines, totals, note, amendments) to the company's Buyers and staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let a Buyer cancel their company's Received orders, setting status to Cancelled with a timeline entry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject Buyer cancellation of non-Received orders, directing them to contact the distributor office.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let a Buyer repeat an order by adding available lines to the basket at current prices, capped at stock, flagging reduced or unavailable lines, without creating an order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return, for staff order listings, all customers' orders with key fields, filterable by customer, date range, and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let staff search customers and view a company's details, addresses, price list, users, status, orders, and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let staff edit Received orders only, limited to quantities, line removal, note, address (same company), and valid delivery date changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall record staff quantity amendments with old/new values, actor, and time, and email the order recipient listing the changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let staff confirm a Received order meeting stock and address conditions, setting status to Confirmed, or reject it listing failing lines.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall send a confirmation email on order confirmation containing order details, totals, address, date, and any pre-confirmation quantity changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall allow only the next valid status transition (Confirmed, Picking, Out for delivery, Delivered, or cancellation), recording a timeline entry and rejecting other changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall send an email when an order moves to Out for delivery status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall require a reason when staff cancel or reject a non-final order, recording it and emailing the recipient.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let staff create an order on behalf of a company under the same pricing, stock, address, and date rules as Buyer orders, marked as staff-created.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall keep inactive companies' existing orders and invoices visible and allow staff to progress, cancel, and invoice their open orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 64,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall export a CSV delivery list for a given date (default today) listing relevant non-Cancelled orders with specified fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 65,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show staff dashboard counts for orders by status, orders due today, and invoice payment statuses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 66,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show the count of Confirmed orders on the staff dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 67,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show the count of failed stock imports since the last success on the staff dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 68,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show the latest stock import result, including failure time and reason, on the dashboard when the most recent import failed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 69,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall create an invoice automatically when an order becomes Delivered, with sequential number, company billing details, order reference, lines, totals, tax, and Unpaid status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 70,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall report an invoice's payment status as Unpaid, Overdue (after a configured period), or Paid once recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 71,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return invoice summaries (number, order, date, total, status) to a Buyer's own company or to staff across all companies.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 72,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff list and view all invoices, filterable by customer and payment status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 73,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall provide invoice PDFs with full invoice details, distributor branding, and company details to the invoice company's Buyers and staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 74,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let staff mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice as Paid with a valid payment date, recording the date and staff user, without storing card data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 75,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators add, edit, and retire products with specified fields, keeping retired products off the catalogue but visible on existing orders/invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 76,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators create, rename, and retire single-level categories and assign products to them, hiding retired categories from Buyers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 77,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators upload a product image, replacing any previous image, restricted to JPEG, PNG, or WebP files up to 10 MB.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 78,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators add and remove vehicle compatibility entries on products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 79,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators create and edit customer companies with specified fields and active/inactive status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 80,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall restrict adding, editing, and removing a company's delivery addresses to staff and administrators, while returning them to the company's Buyers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 81,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators view and change system settings including cutoff time, timezone, non-working dates, delivery limits, thresholds, tax rate, number prefixes, link validity periods, and invoice branding.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 82,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall store and expose creation and last-change actor/time metadata on orders, invoices, companies, users, products, categories, and price lists to administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 83,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall provide a sales report, on-screen and as CSV, for a date range and optional customer filter, summarizing order counts, totals, and product sales from non-Cancelled orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 84,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject an administrator's attempt to deactivate their own account or change their own role, leaving the account unchanged.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}